        "size": 12714823
      },
      "features": [
        "**Updates page** at Settings → Version, in the Morphe style: summary card with installed→latest version pills, a \"N new releases\" line, and feature/fix/optimization count pills, then an expandable timeline with per-category cards, relative dates, and Pre-release/Latest badges.",
        "**Search-as-you-type in Requests.** Typing queries SoulSync's v1 search endpoint and shows real tracks with cover art, album, source and duration. Request stays disabled until you pick a track, so only a real song can be submitted.",
        "**Requests now land on the SoulSync wishlist.** A submitted track is written to the server wishlist, so it appears in the SoulSync web UI and can be tracked there.",
        "**Submitted requests survive restarts.** They are persisted per SoulSync identity and shown in the Requests list instead of vanishing on refresh."
      ],
      "fixes": [
        "**Requests no longer empty themselves after a submit.** The list had treated a session-only endpoint as its source of truth, so a submission appeared for a moment and then disappeared.",
        "**Submits are no longer locked to one music provider.** The app now accepts whatever track identity the server's search returns, instead of refusing anything that was not Spotify. Verified on a Deezer-backed instance.",
        "**Successful wishlist submits no longer show as FAILED.** The app stamped a provenance string as the failure reason and then read it back as a failure; provenance and failure are now separate.",
        "**Updates page no longer opens as a blank grey screen.** Its providers were mounted outside the scoped container, which threw in release builds and rendered an empty screen instead of the page or an error.",
        "**iOS app icon ships again.** The icon is included as bundle icons declared in the Info.plist, which works without an asset-catalog compiler.",
        "**Release version codes no longer roll over.** Beta and nightly build numbers keep increasing instead of wrapping and producing installs the device treats as downgrades."
      ],
      "optimizations": [
        "**Release manifest is regenerated in full on every release** rather than appended to, so it cannot drift, with a daily rebuild as self-heal.",
        "**Manifest fetch no longer reports a stale cached release as confirmed up to date.**"
      ],
